# zlib 1.2.13 — our delta from pristine upstream.
#
# Upstream: https://github.com/madler/zlib/releases/download/v1.2.13/zlib-1.2.13.tar.gz
#           sha256 b3a24de97a8fdbc835b9833169501030b8977031bcb54b3b3ac13740f846ab30
# Apply from sdk/lib/3rdparty/zlib/ with: patch -p1 < vendor-patches/zlib.patch
#
# SCOPE: zlib PROPER IS PRISTINE. Every file that makes up the compression library —
# adler32, crc32, deflate, inflate, inftrees, trees, zutil, gz*, compress, uncompr,
# infback and both public headers — is byte-identical to upstream 1.2.13. Nothing in
# this patch touches bounds checking, allocation, or the inflate/deflate state
# machines. The entire delta is three files under contrib/minizip, the ZIP-archive
# helper that ships alongside zlib.
#
# WHAT IT DOES: minizip has two file backends, a stdio FILE* one (ioapi.c's
# fill_fopen64_filefunc and friends) and a win32-HANDLE one (iowin32.c). ReactOS uses
# only the win32 one, so the stdio half and the zipOpen2/unzOpen2 entry points that
# depend on it are compiled out behind __REACTOS__. unzip.c additionally stops
# NOUNCRYPT from being force-defined, which ENABLES minizip's traditional-PKWARE
# decryption support rather than disabling it — note that direction, it is easy to
# read backwards.
#
# WHY NOT A BUILD FLAG: __REACTOS__ already IS a build flag; what cannot move into the
# build is the choice of WHICH REGIONS it guards, because upstream has no such
# conditionals to switch on. Deleting the stdio backend outright would be a larger
# delta, not a smaller one.
#
# DE-PATCHED 2026-09-20 (was five files, now three):
#   iowin32.c   restored to pristine. It had four `const char* mode_fopen = NULL;`
#               declarations commented out to silence -Wunused-variable. That is a
#               warning, not a portability need, so it moved into the build as
#               `target_compile_options(minizip PRIVATE -Wno-unused-variable)`,
#               scoped to minizip so it cannot hide an unused variable in zlib proper.
#   zip.c       the cosmetic hunk (braces added around a `for` body) is reverted; only
#               the two __REACTOS__ hunks remain.
# Both were pure noise that would have had to be re-applied at every bump.
#
--- a/contrib/minizip/ioapi.c
+++ b/contrib/minizip/ioapi.c
@@ -66,6 +66,7 @@
